  "Thin data shown": "ప్రతి గ్రాఫ్‌కు డేటా పాయింట్ల సంఖ్య 12,000 కంటే ఎక్కువ కాబట్టి, డేటా పాయింట్ల సంఖ్య గరిష్టంగా 12,000 కు పరిమితం చేయబడింది. మీరు మొత్తం డేటాను చూడాలనుకుంటే, తక్కువ లక్ష్య వ్యవధిని సెట్ చేయండి.",
  "Stratify by term (Cyclic)": "పదం ద్వారా స్తరీకరించండి (చక్రీయ)",
  "Facet": "ముఖభాగం",
  "Facet Hover msg": "Plots are split by the selected variable values. Only variables with a Category (Cat) or String (Str) data type can be selected.\nIf only Lv1 or Lv2 is selected, plots are split by the distinct values of the selected variable.\nIf both Lv1 and Lv2 are selected, plots are split by every combination of the two variables' values.\n(If Lv1 has n levels and Lv2 has m levels, n × m plots will be generated.\n Since the number of plots can grow quickly, avoid selecting variables with too many levels,\n or use filters to reduce the number of plots displayed.)\n\nDiv option:\nOn the pages listed below, Div can be selected in addition to Lv1 and Lv2. Its role depends on the page:\n・ RLP, AgP: The selected variable is used for grouping, and data is aggregated or summarized for each variable value.\n・ ScP: Plots are split in the same way as Lv1 and Lv2. Lv1 and Lv2 create vertical sections, while Div creates horizontal sections.\n・ WfP: Waveforms are drawn separately for each value of the selected variable.\n・ MAP: Plots are displayed side by side for each selected variable value (up to 6 panels).\n        Use filters to narrow down the number of values if necessary.\n        This option is available when only one checkbox is selected (i.e., when only [1] is selected).\n",
